parameters.text:
=You are an intake assistant for a smart electricity bill advisory system. Read the raw bill submission below and return ONLY a JSON object (no markdown, no commentary) with these fields:

- tariffCategoryNormalized (string, e.g. "Domestic", "Commercial", "Industrial")
- ratePerUnit (number, calculate as billAmount / unitsConsumed if not explicitly derivable, else null)
- billingMonth (string, MM)
- billingYear (string, YYYY)
- isValid (boolean, true only if accountId, unitsConsumed, billAmount, billingPeriod, and customerEmail are all present and the numeric fields are valid numbers)
- missingFields (array of strings, names of any required fields that are missing or unusable)

Raw bill submission:
Account ID: {{ $json.accountId }}
Customer Name: {{ $json.customerName }}
Customer Email: {{ $json.customerEmail }}
Billing Period: {{ $json.billingPeriod }}
Meter Reading: {{ $json.meterReading }}
Prior Meter Reading: {{ $json.priorMeterReading }}
Units Consumed: {{ $json.unitsConsumed }}
Tariff Category: {{ $json.tariffCategory }}
Bill Amount: {{ $json.billAmount }}

parameters.jsCode:
// Safely parse the AI's structured validation output and merge with the original bill context
const item = $input.item.json;
const raw = item.output || item.text || item.response || '{}';

let parsed = {};
try {
  const cleaned = String(raw).replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();
  parsed = JSON.parse(cleaned);
} catch (e) {
  parsed = { isValid: false, missingFields: ['unparseable_ai_response'] };
}

const original = $('Set Bill Context Data').item.json;

return {
  json: {
    ...original,
    tariffCategoryNormalized: parsed.tariffCategoryNormalized || original.tariffCategory,
    ratePerUnit: parsed.ratePerUnit || null,
    billingMonth: parsed.billingMonth || (original.billingPeriod || '').slice(5, 7),
    billingYear: parsed.billingYear || (original.billingPeriod || '').slice(0, 4),
    isValid: !!parsed.isValid && !!original.customerEmail && !!original.accountId,
    missingFields: parsed.missingFields || []
  }
};

parameters.text:
=You are a smart electricity bill advisor. Based on the anomaly analysis below, write a clear, helpful advisory report (under 180 words) for the customer.

Bill ID: {{ $json.billId }}
Account: {{ $json.accountId }}
Billing Period: {{ $json.billingPeriod }}
Units Consumed: {{ $json.unitsConsumed }} (12-month average: {{ $json.avgUnits }})
Percent Increase vs Average: {{ $json.percentIncreaseVsAvg }}%
Seasonal Increase (same month last year): {{ $json.seasonalIncreasePercent }}%
Tariff Slab Change Detected: {{ $json.tariffSlabJump }}
Anomaly Score: {{ $json.anomalyScore }}/100
Severity: {{ $json.severity }}

Explain in plain language whether this bill looks unusual, the most likely causes (e.g. seasonal appliance use, tariff slab change, possible meter fault, increased occupancy), and 2-3 concrete money-saving or next-step recommendations. If severity is High, recommend requesting a meter inspection. Do NOT include disclaimers about being an AI.

parameters.jsCode:
// Parse the AI advisory output and build the final report + escalation payloads
const item = $input.first().json;
const advisoryText = item.output || item.response || item.text ||
  `We reviewed your latest bill (${item.billId}) and did not detect a significant anomaly in your consumption pattern.`;

const severity = item.severity || 'Normal';
const isEscalationRequired = !!item.isEscalationRequired;

const emailSubject = `Unusual Consumption Alert — Account ${item.accountId} (Bill ${item.billId})`;
const emailBody = advisoryText;

return [{
  json: {
    ...item,
    advisoryText,
    emailSubject,
    emailBody,
    logDate: new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0],
    logTimestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    status: isEscalationRequired ? 'Escalated' : (severity === 'Moderate' ? 'Reviewed - Moderate' : 'Reviewed - Normal')
  }
}];
